<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 3.276 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 3.276 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 3.276 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    342 days   24.14 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    182 days   23.14 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    450 million     35 days</p>
<p>    450 million     34 days</p>
<p>    600 million     20 days</p>
<p>    600 million     15 days</p>
<p>    500 million	5 days</p>
<p>    226 million	3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
